<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Analyze user behavior on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/</link><description>Recent content in Analyze user behavior on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Feature adoption</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/1-adoption/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/1-adoption/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Remember seeing the &amp;ldquo;Ask AI&amp;rdquo; feature on Astronomy Shop product detail pages? We want to understand how our customers are using that feature, including the quick prompts provided below the text input field.
&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../images/ask-ai-astronomy.png" alt="Ask AI feature on Astronomy Shop product details" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Understand feature adoption&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Navigate to the analyses tab of the DXA project, and click into the timeseries &amp;ldquo;AI feature adoption&amp;rdquo;
&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="https://colony-recorder.s3.amazonaws.com/files/2026-03-19/c0716b91-9c74-41f2-9545-dcf6cd46a1fa/ascreenshot_f11164e9f0274895b40466f0b51c8c3e_text_export.jpeg" alt="timeseries with quick prompts" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Frustration</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/2-frustration/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/2-frustration/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Now let&amp;rsquo;s see how the same type of analysis can help us understand if our end users are experiencing friction interacting with the application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Monitor friction&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Return to the Project Analyses and open the Frustration timeseries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explore the chart, data table, and session replay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../images/frustration-timeseries.png" alt="timeseries chart showing three frustration series" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs" data-tabs&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs__list" role="tablist"&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-tab-0" class="tabs__btn is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-panel-0" tabindex="0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;Questions&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-tab-1" class="tabs__btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-panel-1" tabindex="-1" data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;Answers&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-panel-0" class="tabs__panel is-active" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-tab-0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What does this chart tell us?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can you tell why users are expressing frustration?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-panel-1" class="tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-2-analytics-2-frustration-md-1-1--0-tab-1" hidden data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This chart is tracking different types of frustration signals over time - such as rage clicks, errors, and dead clicks. Multiple users are experiencing points of friction!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Did you find the useless &amp;ldquo;Show all reviews&amp;rdquo; button? Some users try to click it, it does nothing, and then the user rage clicks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="https://colony-recorder.s3.amazonaws.com/files/2026-03-19/13f755d5-8819-4d06-83b3-a0f159568b43/ascreenshot_e2b4eaaa95ca43139b275fbe4609f55c_text_export.jpeg" alt="frustration replay" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Funnels</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/3-funnels/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/2-analytics/3-funnels/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;ve seen individual user actions tracked over time, but how do we know if our end users are using our app the way we expect them to?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Explore the funnel&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Return to the Project Analyses and open the Homepage to Order Confirmation funnel. Make sure the chart is filtered to show &amp;ldquo;All users&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This funnel is capturing users who started on the homepage, shopped, and checked out. If users dropped off before the next step, that&amp;rsquo;s captured.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>